<title>USA: AmeriTrade IPO opens strong.</title>
<headline>AmeriTrade IPO opens strong.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of the initial public offering of AmeriTrade Holding Corp opened strongly on Tuesday morning at 16-3/4, up from the initial price of $15.</p>
<p>According to lead underwriter CS First Boston, 2.35 million shares were priced on Monday.</p>
<p>AmeriTrade is a low-cost discount securities broker. The company operates under the names Accutrade, K. Aufhauser, Ceres and eBroker, and derives 85 percent of its revenues from retail discount brokerage, according to Standard &amp; Poor's.</p>
</text>
